{"name":"Head in the Sand","hex":"#ebe2de","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"head in the sand","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of disregarding or denying a problem or threat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/head_in_the_sand"}],"entries":[{"title":"Common ostrich","blocks":[{"text":"The common ostrich, or simply ostrich, is a species of flightless bird native to certain areas of Africa and is the largest living species of bird. The common ostrich is one of two extant species of ostriches, the only living members of the genus Struthio in the ratite group of birds. The other is the Somali ostrich, which has been recognised as a distinct species by BirdLife International since 2014, having been previously considered a distinctive subspecies of ostrich."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Struthio_camelus_-_Etosha_2014_%283%29.jpg/330px-Struthio_camelus_-_Etosha_2014_%283%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_ostrich","wikidata":"Q17592"},{"title":"Head","blocks":[{"text":"A head is the part of an organism which usually includes the ears, brain, forehead, cheeks, chin, eyes, nose, and mouth, each of which aids in various sensory functions such as sight, hearing, smell, and taste. Some very simple animals may not have a head, but many bilaterally symmetric forms do, regardless of size."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Portrait_of_a_Meerkat.jpg/330px-Portrait_of_a_Meerkat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Head","wikidata":"Q23640"},{"title":"Sand","blocks":[{"text":"Sand is a granular material composed of finely divided mineral particles. Sand has various compositions but is usually defined by its grain size. Sand grains are smaller than gravel and coarser than silt. Sand can also refer to a textural class of soil or soil type; i.e., a soil containing more than 85 percent sand-sized particles by mass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg/330px-Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand","wikidata":"Q34679"},{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)","wikidata":"Q9303163"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Struthio_camelus_%28captive%29_in_Jardim_Zool%C3%B3gico_de_Curitiba.jpg/330px-Struthio_camelus_%28captive%29_in_Jardim_Zool%C3%B3gico_de_Curitiba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Struthio_camelus_%28captive%29_in_Jardim_Zool%C3%B3gico_de_Curitiba.jpg/960px-Struthio_camelus_%28captive%29_in_Jardim_Zool%C3%B3gico_de_Curitiba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Struthio_camelus_%28captive%29_in_Jardim_Zool%C3%B3gico_de_Curitiba.jpg/330px-Struthio_camelus_%28captive%29_in_Jardim_Zool%C3%B3gico_de_Curitiba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStruthio_camelus_(captive)_in_Jardim_Zool%C3%B3gico_de_Curitiba.jpg"},{"sr